 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1031 "Evaluating Trigonometric Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1033 3766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050848 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6b88d999-b59b-5a39-b090-40b21de4e2a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073464 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1370" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073464 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $8\\sqrt 3 - 5\\sqrt 3 + \\sqrt 5$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf793c45-6c89-50c8-bb28-d066d2b8342a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073464 #edb/ref 1074 "We can combine the two $\\sqrt{3}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8\\sqrt{3} - 5\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{5} &=  \\\\\n(8 - 5)\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{5} &=  \\\\\n&= 3\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073663 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073663 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $2\\sqrt[3]{5} +5 \\sqrt{10} -3 \\sqrt[3]{40}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073663 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5202e06-b6a8-5d74-a395-fe7c56b8e9bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073663 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we use the product rule for radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt[3]{40} &= \\sqrt[3]{8 \\cdot 5} = \\sqrt[3]{8} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{5} = 2\\sqrt[3]{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sqrt[3]{5} + 5\\sqrt{10} - 3\\sqrt[3]{40} &=  \\\\\n2\\sqrt[3]{5} + 5\\sqrt{10} - 3(2\\sqrt[3]{5}) &=  \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt[3]{5} + 5\\sqrt{10} - 6\\sqrt[3]{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{5}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sqrt[3]{5} + 5\\sqrt{10} - 6\\sqrt[3]{5} &=  \\\\\n5\\sqrt{10} + (2\\sqrt[3]{5} - 6\\sqrt[3]{5}) &=  \\\\\n5\\sqrt{10} + (2 - 6)\\sqrt[3]{5} &=  \\\\\n&= 5\\sqrt{10} - 4\\sqrt[3]{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073664 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073664 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $3\\sqrt{80} -8\\sqrt{5}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073664 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c1f1d037-45a6-5e72-a735-0c0512290120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073664 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we use the product rule for radicals to simplify $\\sqrt{80}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt{80} &= \\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{16} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 4\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\sqrt{80} - 8\\sqrt{5} &=  \\\\\n3(4\\sqrt{5}) - 8\\sqrt{5} &=  \\\\\n&= 12\\sqrt{5} - 8\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can combine the two $\\sqrt{5}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12\\sqrt{5} - 8\\sqrt{5} &=  \\\\\n(12 - 8)\\sqrt{5} &=  \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073788 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073788 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073788 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073788 #edb/ref 1039 "Simplifying Expressions Containing Cube Roots" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073788 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073788 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1a31c2b6-585a-5715-98f8-4b82605f4c22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073789 #edb/ref 1